INTERFACE

1. Declared using interface keyword.

2. A class uses implements to implement an interface.

3. Abstract methods in an interface are implemented
   by the implementing class.

4. Cannot create an interface object directly.

   Vehicle v = new Vehicle();  // ❌

5. Interface does NOT have a normal constructor.

6. Variables in an interface are automatically:
   public static final

7. Methods can be:
   → public abstract (traditional abstract methods)
   → default
   → static
   → private (Java 9+)

8. A class can implement MULTIPLE interfaces.

9. Interface supports multiple inheritance.

   class HyundaiCar implements Vehicle, Engine {
   }